<h1><span data-field="title" data-format="default">font_sdf_spread</span></h1>
<p>This function is used to change the spread value of an <a href="font_enable_sdf.htm">SDF-enabled font</a>. The spread limits how much <a href="font_enable_effects.htm">font effects</a> can spread from a glyph&#39;s edge.</p>
<p>The spread value is the distance (in pixels) that the signed distance field extends from the edge of each glyph. The spread can be between 2 and 32 pixels (inclusive), and the default is 8.</p>
<p>This is also useful for running custom shaders on your text, as a larger spread value will allow for effects with larger radii (such as glows). However a larger spread value will mean that the font will take up more space on the texture page. In contrast, a smaller spread value will save texture space, and also improve rendering precision.</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-field="title" data-format="default">font_sdf_spread</span>(ind, spread);</p>
<table>
<colgroup>
<col/>
<col/>
<col/>
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th>Argument</th>
<th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>ind</td>
<td><span data-keyref="Type_Asset_Font"><a target="_blank" href="../../../../The_Asset_Editors/Fonts.htm">Font Asset</a></span></td>
<td>The index of the font (must be <a href="font_enable_sdf.htm">SDF-enabled</a>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>spread</td>
<td><span data-keyref="Type_Real"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">Real</a></span></td>
<td>The new spread value, between 2 and 32 pixels (inclusive)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_Void">N/A</span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">new_font = font_add(&quot;STENCIL.TTF&quot;, 32, false, false, 32, 128);<br/>
font_enable_sdf(new_font, true);<br/>
<span data-field="title" data-format="default">font_sdf_spread</span>(new_font, 16);
</p>
<p>This will load a font from an included TTF file, enable SDF for it and set its spread value to 16 pixels.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
